# -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- --
# CPU POWER LIMIT WITHOUT A PASSWORD FOR THE wheel GROUP.
#
# Cogwheel sets the limit of the current power profile through
# /usr/local/sbin/df-limit-mocy (sbin/df-limit-mocy in the repo), which needs
# root for ryzenadj. The shell calls it on every profile change and once a
# minute, so it has to go without a password - and without a syslog line and
# a PAM session each time, or the log would get one entry a minute.
#
# Only that one root-owned script, which validates its arguments. Never point
# a rule like this at a file in the home directory - whoever can edit the file
# gets root.
#
# Installation (root) - ALWAYS through visudo -c first, a broken file in
# /etc/sudoers.d locks sudo out completely:
#   install -o root -g root -m 0755 sbin/df-limit-mocy /usr/local/sbin/
#   visudo -cf sudoers/dark-fantasy-moc
#   install -o root -g root -m 0440 sudoers/dark-fantasy-moc /etc/sudoers.d/
# -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- --
Defaults!/usr/local/sbin/df-limit-mocy !syslog, !pam_session
%wheel ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/sbin/df-limit-mocy
